# Template for the GitHub `production` environment secret K8S_RUNTIME_ENV.
# One KEY=VALUE per line, value verbatim (no quotes, no export). Blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. scripts/materialize-k8s-runtime-secrets.sh turns it into every Kubernetes runtime
# secret; check-k3s-runtime-secret.sh rejects an empty, short, CHANGE_ME or non-PgBouncer value.
#
# Most values are the same as /etc/warptalk/.env.production on the compose hosts. Two differences:
#   * every *_CONNECTION_STRING / *_DSN must point at the in-cluster PgBouncer:
#     warptalk-postgres-pooler-rw.warptalk-data.svc.cluster.local:5432
#   * Redis__ConnectionString / ConnectionStrings__Redis use the Sentinel service
#     warptalk-redis.warptalk-data.svc.cluster.local:26379 (serviceName=mymaster)
#
# STRIPE_*, LIVEKIT_*, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_*, CARTESIA_* may be left out here: the
# release job overlays the GitHub secrets/vars the compose release already uses.

# --- warptalk-runtime (deploy/k3s/runtime-secret-contract.json) ---
